They basically have started doing it — just not as one opinionated “startup OS” yet.

The biggest update is that **Shopify for ChatGPT now explicitly says you can turn a small-business idea into an ecommerce site conversationally: describe what you sell, create the store, add products, manage inventory, orders, discounts and analytics.** ([OpenAI][1])

At the same time OpenAI has separately shipped:

* ChatGPT apps that run inside the conversation and can be suggested contextually. ([OpenAI][2])
* recurring Scheduled tasks, including hourly runs on eligible paid plans and integrations with connected apps. ([OpenAI Help Center][3])
* native Shopify product discovery in ChatGPT. ([OpenAI Help Center][4])
* agentic checkout/commerce infrastructure via ACP. ([OpenAI][5])
* business data analysis and dashboards through the new Data agent. ([OpenAI][6])
* financial research/data products, while deliberately stopping short of personalized investment advice. ([OpenAI][7])

So your intuition is right:

> **The primitives required to go “idea → company → sales → operations → capital” are appearing extremely quickly.**

What's missing is the **entrepreneurial control loop**.

